#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:10
msgid "Golden Standard Methodology"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:12
msgid ""
"**Purpose** The golden_standard methodology provides comprehensive "
"validation through explicit, manual verification of all input data and "
"output results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:15
msgid ""
"**Scope** This methodology extends basic_check with rigorous manual "
"verification of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:18
msgid "All ``pdf_blks`` and ``txt_blks`` input files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:19
msgid "Complete data extraction verification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:20
msgid "Explicit confirmation that no data is missing from results"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:22
msgid ""
"**Covered File Types** - All files covered by basic_check methodology - "
"Additional verification of input block files (``pdf_blks``, ``txt_blks``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:26
msgid "**Protocol Steps**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:28
msgid "**Complete basic_check protocol** (all steps)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:29
msgid "**Input Block Verification**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:31
msgid "Manually review every ``pdf_blk`` and ``txt_blk`` file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:32
msgid ""
"Verify that all relevant data from input blocks is captured in "
"``results.pkl``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:33
msgid "Explicitly confirm no data is omitted or incorrectly parsed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:35
msgid "**Log Analysis**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:37
msgid "Verify that ``.log.csv`` contains only true anomalies or is empty"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:38
msgid "Each warning in the log must be reviewed and confirmed as legitimate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:40
msgid "**Comprehensive Data Validation**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:42
msgid "Cross-reference every data point in output files with source blocks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:43
msgid "Verify data consistency across all output formats (CSV, YAML, pickle)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:45
msgid "**Edge Case Verification**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:47
msgid "Check handling of unusual data formats or structures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:48
msgid "Verify error handling and logging for problematic inputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:50
msgid ""
"**Trust Level** This methodology provides **strong certification** - it "
"represents thorough manual verification that all data is correctly "
"processed and no information is lost during extraction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:53
msgid ""
"**Applicable Context** Use this methodology for: - Release candidate "
"validation - Critical data processing verification - Situations requiring"
" high confidence in data accuracy - Validation of core algorithm "
"functionality"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:60
msgid ""
"**Relationship to basic_check** The golden_standard methodology includes "
"and extends all basic_check requirements, providing a superset of "
"validation guarantees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:64
msgid "Supported paths"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:66
msgid ""
"This methodology covers the same files as ``basic check`` -- it is that "
"protocol plus the manual verification described above, not a different "
"subject -- so the patterns are the same, and what changes is what a grant"
" on them claims. All patterns are relative to the root of the repository "
"the granted file lives in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:71
msgid "``tests/formats/**/out/*.csv``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:72
msgid ""
"The tabular reference output of a format's test suite in a **formats "
"repository**. A golden standard grant here claims more than that the "
"values look reasonable: every one of them was cross-referenced against "
"the blocks it was extracted from, and ``.log.csv`` was read line by line "
"and found to contain only anomalies confirmed as genuine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:77
msgid "``tests/formats/**/out/*.yaml``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:78
msgid "The non-tabular output of the same run, verified to the same standard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:80
msgid "``tests/formats/**/pages/**``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:81
msgid ""
"The per-page fixtures: the blocks the extraction saw, and the result it "
"reached. This is where the additional claim actually rests -- a golden "
"standard grant says every block was reviewed and that nothing relevant "
"present in the page is missing from the result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/golden_standard.rst:87
msgid ""
"As with ``basic check``, these paths describe a **formats repository**, "
"and the variant level between a format and its outputs is optional -- "
"hence ``**`` rather than ``*``."
msgstr ""

